{"evidence":["Reviewed the implemented routing in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:168-232` and the new parameter definitions in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:171-209`.","Ran `cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_feeding_pathway`: all 7 pathway tests passed.","Ran `cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking test_budget_component_labels_cover_all_element_bearing_fields`: passed, confirming `animal.reserve_g` is covered by the N/C budget diagnostics.","Ran `cargo test -p tank_core`: the only failing tests were `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` (`threshold_events_emit_with_cause_codes`, `threshold_events_are_deduplicated_per_day`); focused shrimp-routing and budget tests passed."],"findings_or_gaps":["Blocking: the new shrimp routing parameters and reserve pool are not validated before simulation. `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:186-232` assumes `shrimp_assimilation_efficiency` is in-range and that respiration + excretion + growth sums to 1.0, but `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:147-181` does not check those fields and also does not check `animal.reserve_g` for non-negativity. Because `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:183-186` relies on `enforce_invariants()` during load, a hand-edited save or future preset can silently create/delete mass and violate the conservation contract this bead is supposed to guarantee.","Completeness/docs mismatch: the implementation adds a direct shrimp excretion-carbon path to DOC in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:210-212`, but the phase-1 routing docs still say consumer dissolved excretion goes to TAN and explicitly say there is no direct consumer routing to DOC/DON in phase 1 (`docs/ROUTING.md:67-72`, `docs/scientific_inventory.md:122-124`). The code and the authoritative routing contract need to match."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Add invariant enforcement for `shrimp_assimilation_efficiency`, `shrimp_respiration_fraction_of_assimilated`, `shrimp_excretion_fraction_of_assimilated`, `shrimp_growth_fraction_of_assimilated`, `shrimp_o2_per_mg_c_respired`, and `animal.reserve_g`, with rejection when bounds or sum rules are violated.","Add regression coverage proving malformed v4 saves / invalid process params are rejected, so conservation does not depend only on the default TOML values.","Either update the routing/scientific docs to bless the new excreted-carbon DOC path, or change the implementation to follow the current documented phase-1 contract."],"outcome":"request_changes"}